    "https://www.msoe.edu/the-msoe-mindset/career-connections-center/": {
      "title": "Milwaukee School of Engineering",
      "description": "Career Connections Center | MSOE Skip to Main Content Milwaukee School of Engineering Secondary Navigation Visit/Apply Partners Alumni Giving Resources For… Future Students Current Students Parent & Family Faculty & Staff Employers Search Menu Site Navigation About MSOE Expand Navigation Who We Are Mission, Vision and Values Strategic Plan Inclusion & Belonging K-12 STEM at MSOE News Careers at MSOE Commencement Admissions & Aid Expand Navigation Undergraduate Admissions International Admissions Graduate Admissions Transfer Admissions Why Choose MSOE? Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships ROAR Visit MSOE Academics Expand Navigation How We Teach Undergraduate Degrees Graduate Degrees Minors Certificates Center for Professional Education Departments Study Abroad High School Programs Campus Experience Expand Navigation Living at MSOE Our Campus Campus Life Student Organizations Athletics Campus and Community Resources Dean of Students Event Calendar The MSOE Mindset Expand Navigation Developing the MSOE Mindset Student Success Stories Employment Outcomes Career Connections Center Preparing for Success Career Connections Center The MSOE Mindset Career Connections Center Developing the MSOE Mindset Student Success Stories Employment Outcomes Career Connections Center Preparing for Success Home The MSOE Mindset Career Connections Center Career Connections Center We want to help you find a career path that will lead to a successful, happy future. The Career Connections Center works hard to make your internship and full-time job search as easy as possible. Not only do we bring employers right on campus to recruit you, we can also help you be their candidate of choice. Students Find valuable guides and examples to help you with your internship and full-time job search, resume, cover letter, Handshake and LinkedIn, interview skills, career fair prep and so much more. Visit the Career Connections Center website Alumni As an alumni, assistance from the Career Connections Center is always available. Whether you’re still looking for your first-full-time job after graduation, looking for a new position, company, or industry, or making a complete career change, we’re happy to help. Visit the Career Connections Center website Employers Thank you for your interest in MSOE students and alumni – we invite you to recruit at MSOE for your internship and full-time job opportunities. Visit the Career Connections Center website Faculty & Staff Learn about how the Career Connections Center helps students and alumni gain valuable employment opportunities while at MSOE, a rewarding career upon graduation, and receive a significant ROI for their hard work earning their degree. Visit the Career Connections Center website Prospective Students & Families The Career Connections Center is one of the MSOE advantages. At MSOE, students and alumni get more out of their degree. More personal attention. More practical experience. More career power. And the advantage is measurable: Just consider our enviable 96% graduate outcomes rate and $77,161 average starting salary (ranked #17 \"Best U.S. College for High Salaries\" by the Wall Street Journal). Visit the Career Connections Center website Contact Information Career Connections Center 1025 N. Broadway CC-370 Milwaukee, WI 53202 (414) 277-7120 career-connections-center@msoe.edu Footer Navigation Employee Directory Raider Shop Library Grohmann Museum Athletics & Recreation Facilities 91.7 WMSE For Employers Support MSOE Milwaukee School of Engineering MSOE University 1025 North Broadway Milwaukee, WI 53202-3109 (800) 332-6763 explore@msoe.edu MSOE is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission (800) 621-7440, ( www.ncahlc.org ). Additional program accreditation includes the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET, the Applied and Natural Science Accreditation Commission of ABET, ( www.abet.org ), Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE), Commission on Accreditation of Allied Health Education Programs (CAAHEP) and Accreditation Council for Business Schools and Programs (ACBSP). Connect With MSOE Facebook Instagram Twitter Linkedin YouTube Vimeo Back To Top Menu Search submit Mobile Site Navigation About MSOE Expand Navigation Who We Are Mission, Vision and Values Strategic Plan Inclusion & Belonging K-12 STEM at MSOE News Careers at MSOE Commencement Admissions & Aid Expand Navigation Undergraduate Admissions International Admissions Graduate Admissions Transfer Admissions Why Choose MSOE? Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships ROAR Visit MSOE Academics Expand Navigation How We Teach Undergraduate Degrees Graduate Degrees Minors Certificates Center for Professional Education Departments Study Abroad High School Programs Campus Experience Expand Navigation Living at MSOE Our Campus Campus Life Student Organizations Athletics Campus and Community Resources Dean of Students Event Calendar The MSOE Mindset Expand Navigation Developing the MSOE Mindset Student Success Stories Employment Outcomes Career Connections Center Preparing for Success Mobile Secondary Navigation Visit/Apply Partners Alumni Giving Resources For… Future Students Current Students Parent & Family Faculty & Staff Employers MSOE University 1025 North Broadway Milwaukee, WI 53202-3109 (800) 332-6763 explore@msoe.edu Footer Navigation Employee Directory Raider Shop Library Grohmann Museum Athletics & Recreation Facilities 91.7 WMSE For Employers Support MSOE Connect With MSOE Facebook Instagram Twitter Linkedin YouTube Vimeo"
