    "https://www.msoe.edu/about-msoe/careers-at-msoe/student-employment/": {
      "title": "Milwaukee School of Engineering",
      "description": "Student Employment | MSOE Skip to Main Content Milwaukee School of Engineering Secondary Navigation Visit/Apply Partners Alumni Giving Resources For… Future Students Current Students Parent & Family Faculty & Staff Employers Search Menu Site Navigation About MSOE Expand Navigation Who We Are Mission, Vision and Values Strategic Plan Inclusion & Belonging K-12 STEM at MSOE News Careers at MSOE Commencement Admissions & Aid Expand Navigation Undergraduate Admissions International Admissions Graduate Admissions Transfer Admissions Why Choose MSOE? Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships ROAR Visit MSOE Academics Expand Navigation How We Teach Undergraduate Degrees Graduate Degrees Minors Certificates Center for Professional Education Departments Study Abroad High School Programs Campus Experience Expand Navigation Living at MSOE Our Campus Campus Life Student Organizations Athletics Campus and Community Resources Dean of Students Event Calendar The MSOE Mindset Expand Navigation Developing the MSOE Mindset Student Success Stories Employment Outcomes Career Connections Center Preparing for Success Student Employment Careers at MSOE Student Employment Faculty Positions Staff Positions Student Employment FAQs Student Employment Application Process Academic Year Opportunities Summer Opportunities Home About MSOE Careers at MSOE Student Employment Student Employment Working on the MSOE campus is both rewarding and fun! Looking for a campus job to offset the cost of college? Or maybe you just want more spending money. MSOE provides many opportunities for campus jobs for students as well as Work-Study jobs (a federally subsidized hourly wage job program) for qualified students. To qualify for student employment during the academic year, students are required to take at least six undergraduate credits or three graduate credits during each term of the academic year. To qualify for student employment during the summer, students are required to be registered for at least six undergraduate credits or three graduate credits for the upcoming fall term. Positions designated as \"Work-Study\" are only available to students who have been awarded federal Work-Study. For more information on federal Work-Study, please contact our Financial Aid department at 414-277-7223 or finaid@msoe.edu . Positions that do not indicate they are Work-Study positions are available to all MSOE students. Click on Academic Year Opportunities to see student jobs available during the Academic Year. Click on Summer Opportunities to see student jobs available during the summer term (Work-Study rules do not apply during the summer). Contact Information Financial Aid Office 1025 North Broadway CC301 Milwaukee, WI 53202 414-277-7223 finaid@msoe.edu Office Hours: Monday-Friday: 8am - 4:30pm Contact Information Human Resources Department 1025 N. Broadway Milwaukee, WI 53202 414-277-7132 hr@msoe.edu f. 414-277-2233 TimeClock Plus (TCP) Student Training TCP is the time and attendance system utilized by MSOE. TCP Quick Reference Guide for Students TCP Training Video for Students Footer Navigation Employee Directory Raider Shop Library Grohmann Museum Athletics & Recreation Facilities 91.7 WMSE For Employers Support MSOE Milwaukee School of Engineering MSOE University 1025 North Broadway Milwaukee, WI 53202-3109 (800) 332-6763 explore@msoe.edu MSOE is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission (800) 621-7440, ( www.ncahlc.org ). Additional program accreditation includes the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET, the Applied and Natural Science Accreditation Commission of ABET, ( www.abet.org ), Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE), Commission on Accreditation of Allied Health Education Programs (CAAHEP) and Accreditation Council for Business Schools and Programs (ACBSP). Connect With MSOE Facebook Instagram Twitter Linkedin YouTube Vimeo Back To Top Menu Search submit Mobile Site Navigation About MSOE Expand Navigation Who We Are Mission, Vision and Values Strategic Plan Inclusion & Belonging K-12 STEM at MSOE News Careers at MSOE Commencement Admissions & Aid Expand Navigation Undergraduate Admissions International Admissions Graduate Admissions Transfer Admissions Why Choose MSOE? Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships ROAR Visit MSOE Academics Expand Navigation How We Teach Undergraduate Degrees Graduate Degrees Minors Certificates Center for Professional Education Departments Study Abroad High School Programs Campus Experience Expand Navigation Living at MSOE Our Campus Campus Life Student Organizations Athletics Campus and Community Resources Dean of Students Event Calendar The MSOE Mindset Expand Navigation Developing the MSOE Mindset Student Success Stories Employment Outcomes Career Connections Center Preparing for Success Mobile Secondary Navigation Visit/Apply Partners Alumni Giving Resources For… Future Students Current Students Parent & Family Faculty & Staff Employers MSOE University 1025 North Broadway Milwaukee, WI 53202-3109 (800) 332-6763 explore@msoe.edu Footer Navigation Employee Directory Raider Shop Library Grohmann Museum Athletics & Recreation Facilities 91.7 WMSE For Employers Support MSOE Connect With MSOE Facebook Instagram Twitter Linkedin YouTube Vimeo"
